    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "layout.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Keep visual_row_count pub(crate). Change only the width step. A U+200B scalar adds no width. A line break still adds no width. Every other scalar still adds 1. A tab still uses the tab width. Do not add U+200C, U+200D, or U+FEFF. Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch is_line_break or visible_line_range. The existing test a_unicode_line_break_has_no_width stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_zero_width_space_adds_no_row checks visual_row_count of ab plus U+200B, columns 2, and tab width 4 is 1. visual_row_count of ab with the same columns is 1. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
